# API overview

The generated service uses FastAPI with the Pokerlost JSON envelope and standard bearer header
authorization over HTTPS.

Every business operation is `POST /<operationId>` with one lowerCamelCase verb name. Public and
protected input use the pure JSON `PokerlostRequest`; protected calls additionally carry
`Authorization: Bearer <access-token>`. Every business result uses `PokerlostResponse`.

`GET /` and `GET /getOpenApi` are public bodyless infrastructure endpoints; the latter returns the
raw OpenAPI document. The pristine service contains no business route, scope value, or concrete
token verifier.

Read `docs/api/operation-contract.md` for operation rules,
`docs/api/pokerlost-response.md` for the response invariant,
`docs/api/header-authorization.md` for exact scopes and local verification, and
`docs/api/openapi-and-sdk.md` for publication/generation.
